+
+## Independent review remediation — round 1 of 5
+
+Input: task-1-review.md; base e5fe53f99099937a5e4ca9eba3373e232e73176c. Addressed Important1/2 and Minor3/4 within Task1 only.
+
+Page/dump relationship is now exact `b"\n".join(ordered_retained_page_bytes)`. Single-page dumps equal page bytes; no normalization or omitted content. LF separator preserves page bytes deterministically. Retained page hashes, exact resource ordering and resolved next-marker checks precede projection. Before sweep scanning, each readable aggregate must equal this projection. Independent branch/PR collision and body/comment mention omission tests now refuse at the named surface's `page projection` diagnostic. Positive pagination uses separate source pages, updates aggregate and actual sweep report/readability, and binds a freshly reviewed canonical payload digest. This is internal consistency, not channel authentication.
+
+Parsed retained JSON must be an object before field access. Claim user must also be an object. Receipt pages must be a list of objects; review occurrences must be a list of objects with proper string surface/nonnegative integer offset/known disposition before sorting. Malformed valid JSON arrays/scalars/null and wrong user/receipt/reviewer structures consistently raise InitAllocationError with source-specific diagnostic. No broad AttributeError swallowing replaces validation.
+
+Noncoverage separately requires `acquisition trust`, as well as remote freshness, independent clones and allocation-versus-authorization. Added isolated checks for each raw claim field, literal claim body, missing acquisition, successful-but-wrong acquisition resource, contradictory channel attestation, actual duplicate framework input paths, unreconciled body occurrence and competing seat claims with matching response. Every negative resets to valid fixture, updates exact hashes/digests, snapshots bundle bytes and asserts the intended source diagnostic. Renamed earlier overstated combined tests to their actual single checks. Validation is split into readable `_validate_claim`, `_validate_gather`, `_validate_review`, and object helpers; test multi-action statements split into separate lines.
+
