+  "title": "badf init: require a reviewed published WP allocation before intake",
+  "problem": "## Measured defect and bounded proposal\n\nAt BADF `b9936e591530a74f919a86c80934b575c3a231e3`, `scripts/badf_gate.py:next_wp_id()` scans only local landed `work/` directories. It returns WP-2026-0160, already occupied by remote branch `wp/WP-2026-0160-mas-std-gap-analysis` / open PR #364 (head `50459d2634de8b87837186d59f80c4cb95e26126`). Intake also writes target files before permissively creating the WP directory.\n\nThis blocks governed BizTrust intake: https://github.com/bstBizEra/biztrust_ib/issues/71. Bera's decision there authorizes BADF-DEM-0146 for BizTrust only at the existing framework pin. It does not authorize this upstream implementation.\n\n## Outcome and scope\n\nMake intake require an explicit, published, independently reconciled allocation before any target mutation. Proposed interface:\n\n`badf init <intent> --work-package WP-2026-NNNN --allocation <record.json>`\n\nBoth arguments are required; no silent landed-only max+1 fallback. Update CLI callers, documentation, contracts/schemas and tests together.\n\nScope: intake allocation evidence, offline validation using existing sweep logic, shared-checkout concurrency, bounded failure recovery, docs/callers/tests. Anticipated change class C3 because gate/controller code is affected; final classification follows existing routing.\n\nOut of scope: runtime/release/deployment/product status, G00 approval, global allocation service, new network dependencies, placeholder ledger entries, monkeypatches, merging unrelated work, and the separately measured demand-status enforcement gap.\n\n## Allocation evidence contract\n\nBind exact WP ID, framework repository/revision and executed controller/schema identities, target repository/baseline, demand ID/file digest, claimant, published claim URL/comment identity/author/timestamps/retained content digest, retained API acquisition evidence, sweep input/report digests and completeness/capture observations, common checkout/worktree inventory, active-seat identities and explicit unpublished/unpushed claim disclosures, independent reviewer/reconciliation decision and exact reviewed digest, and non-coverage.\n\nCaller JSON or matching hashes establish neither GitHub identity nor global exclusivity. Retain source evidence and independent channel verification. Published issue claims remain the binding mechanism; independent clones remain invisible.\n\nRequire readable nonblank ledger, branches, PR file lists, bodies and comments; complete successful pagination/gathering, known-present positive controls and prescribed sentinel exclusions. Recompute claim-shaped occupancy using existing sweep semantics. Prose remains a mention requiring explicit reconciliation, not a regex-derived allocation. Refuse missing, ambiguous, forged, rejected/superseded or conflicting allocation evidence.\n\nBind freshness to reviewed framework/controller/schema, demand, target HEAD/status/AGENTS, claim and acquired sweep evidence. Re-sweep/reconcile affected drift; do not invent an arbitrary expiry interval.\n\n## Concurrency, mutation and recovery\n\nUse the verified Git common directory for clone-wide reservation/locking across sibling worktrees. Serialize both WP reservation and target/project/registry uniqueness, so two different IDs cannot register the same target or overwrite shared metadata. Define deterministic lock order.\n\nPrepare and schema-validate all generated outputs before writes. Inside the locks, reread and revalidate target baseline/cleanliness/AGENTS, absence of instance, project/registry uniqueness, framework/controller/schema, demand and allocation evidence before first target mutation.\n\nReject existing WP paths, symlinks and partial/foreign reservations. Retain allocation evidence and bind its digest in the WP and init receipt. Preserve existing AGENTS behavior and unsigned HUMAN_REQUIRED G00.\n\nOn partial failure, retain diagnostic receipt and held reservation. Never recursively delete a namespace after ownership or expected bytes drift. Recovery must be a named bounded action with exact ownership/content checks; never blindly retry.\n\n## Acceptance and meaningful negative tests\n\n- Occupied remote branch/PR/competing claim refuses despite a lower landed maximum.\n- Explicit allocation is consistent across WP, target state, registry, receipt and dossier.\n- Missing/blank/undecodable/truncated or incomplete gathers, missing anchors/disclosures, harmless prose versus competing claim, malformed/sentinel/traversal IDs, wrong bindings, forged attribution and edited/stale evidence are covered.\n- Same-ID contenders in one clone/sibling worktrees and different-ID/same-target contenders cannot both succeed; registry writes are coordinated.\n- Inject preflight-to-write drift and partial failures; conservative recovery preserves evidence and foreign changes.\n- Every preflight refusal leaves protected target, existing WP, registry and lockfile bytes unchanged.\n- Positive case preserves existing AGENTS and unsigned G00 hold.\n- Independent review and composed-result targeted tests, repository gate and mandatory full suite must run before implementation acceptance.\n\n## Separate observed finding\n\nIntake calls load_demand(), which checks human-shaped authorized_by for issue records but does not require status AUTHORIZED. Track that independently; do not silently expand this allocator package.\n\n## Governed route\n\nFreeze source; repeat full sweep and active-seat disclosures; publish reconciled demand/WP claims before binding IDs; export exact demand; obtain human authorization and approved implementation WP; implement/review/test under existing controls; land approved candidate; explicitly reconcile its new BADF revision with BizTrust authorization; then freshly allocate BizTrust intake and generate its own G00 request.\n\nDiscovery/preparation is allowed by the existing demand doctrine. This proposal supplies no human authorization, approved implementation WP, G07 PASS, merge authority or gate approval.\n\n## Independent preparation review\n\nDesign author: /root/allocator_correction_design. Independent read-only challenge: /root/allocator_independent_review. Both disclosed zero unpublished/unpushed ID claims. Review disposition APPROVE_WITH_CONDITIONS for proposal preparation only; the common-directory/target concurrency, integrity-versus-authenticity, locked rechecks, conservative recovery and complete CLI update conditions are incorporated above.\n\nBaseline source/doctrine inspection performed. Implementation/code review/new tests/repository gate/full suite for this proposed change: NOT_RUN. No implementation artifact exists. No demand/WP ID is bound in this source body; the subsequent allocation and export packet will hold those identities.\n\nDisposition: bounded correction proposal prepared; upstream implementation HUMAN_REQUIRED under its own exact demand and approved WP.",
+  "recorded_at": "2026-10-10T18:10:00Z",
+  "provenance": "EXPORTED_FROM_SOURCE",
+  "status": "AUTHORIZED",
+  "note": "Named human Vily / OP / Mr. Ounekhamvilay PHIMMASONE, self-stated account @pvily, acting as human session operator and accountable owner of WP-2026-0161, explicitly agreed in the same ChatGPT session at 2026-10-10T19:53:33Z. Agent transcription: https://github.com/bstBizEra/badf/issues/365#issuecomment-6101568587. Shared connector authorship is not personal GitHub authorship or independent account-identity verification. This promotes only authorization metadata for the exact original OPEN export cc6c857a21b84ce76ea5f33dc4c58c29d46a243d7ed3fe963a9d51e95ee28e99. Exact plan SHA-256 4cedbb88f063a30beaf26fead8ab432e7edfb3b05ffd04bcb73c33b48c560205; baseline b9936e591530a74f919a86c80934b575c3a231e3; policy epoch BADF-2026-08-25; C3. Scoped isolated allocator implementation, tests and independent review only; Issue366 excluded. No G07/C3 gate, acceptance, merge, changed BizTrust pin, G00, runtime, release or deployment approval. Original source, body, export timestamp, recorded_at and scope preserved.",
